WEBVTT

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.650
Is that true?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.180
Has Nobunaga really 
arrived in Kyoto?

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.190
Yeah.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.130
Yoshimoto spent years preparing for it.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.960
And Nobunaga accomplished it without preparation,
 with just twenty mounted soldiers.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.120
He went into Azai and Rokkaku 
territories with just twenty soldiers?

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.480
Yeah.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:31.200
He is more stupid than bold.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.090
A true fool.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.790
But not only did he present himself 
to the shogun, he even received a sword.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:40.150
From the shogun?

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.020
He is a mystery.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.490
Still,

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:49.190
with Dosan Saito no longer alive, 
Nobunaga is nothing to fear.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.070
It is a good time for the 
Yoshimoto army to move out.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.960
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.960
<b>Battle of Okehazama</b>

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:14.260
It doesn't say anything 
about Imagawa-san.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.970
All right!

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:37.650
Huh?

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.030
Mr. Horsie's so clean today!

00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:46.620
Th-That's because I have 
taken care of him.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:49.030
Oh yeah?

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.590
Huh? You're...

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.910
I haven't seen you before.

00:01:58.910 --> 00:01:59.680
Are you new?

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:03.890
Yes! Tokichiro Kinoshita 
is the name.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:04.820
I see.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.140
Thanks a lot.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.090
Okay, I'm heading off to see my friends.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.100
Got it?

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.060
I want you to cooperate.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:24.950
Got it.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.470
My lord!

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.620
It's Tsune-chan.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.630
You really must not leave the castle
 at a time like this!

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:40.250
My lord, do you not understand the situation
 the Oda family is in right now?!

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.250
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:42.100
I'm sorry.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.190
Okay then, I'm counting on you.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:46.430
Leave it to me!

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.670
Oh, wait!

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.770
Let's choose a leader.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:52.390
"Leader"?

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.310
"Leader"?

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:55.610
I choose you!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.280
Eh?

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:01.230
You have a leader-ish face.

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:04.280
I want you in charge.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.200
Your name?

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:06.120
Masa.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.120
Masa. You're the leader.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:11.040
Right.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.380
What is a "leader"?

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:13.980
Who knows...

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:14.670
My lord!

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:19.750
This is not the time to be 
having fun with the villagers.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.280
We must strategize immediately.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.310
Tsune-chan!

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.220
I'm thinking, too! 
Do you think I'm not?

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:31.260
Forgive me.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:35.120
And what are your thoughts?

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.380
I'm hungry...

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.250
Hey, Kichou, let's go home.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.870
You get hungry 
so quickly, my lord.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:50.560
Knowing my lord,
he's sure to have a plan!

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.310
Yeah.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.770
<i>That night, Oda's men 
gathered for a meeting</i>

00:03:56.770 --> 00:04:01.740
<i>to discuss how they should 
best fight Imagawa.</i>

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:04.440
We must prepare for war!

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:09.680
Forty thousand of Imagawa's men
 may attack Kiyosu here within two days!

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:15.140
But at best, we will only 
have three thousand men.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.120
We would not stand a chance 
with such a difference in size.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.910
Then do you suggest we surrender?

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:23.380
Perhaps we should retreat to the 
castle and await their move.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.940
You propose that we allow 
them to lay siege on us

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.200
when we would not 
receive reinforcements?

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:26.200
My lord!

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:31.630
You are the supreme commander 
of the Oda family.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:36.290
Should you choose war,
 we will obey.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.510
What are your thoughts?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:52.770
All I can say is this:

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.140
eat well, sleep well!

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.620
That's all!

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.900
Well then, everyone, good night.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:17.000
That damn lord...

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.570
I'm speechless.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.880
It seems this is the end 
of the Oda family.

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:28.040
Here you are, sir.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:35.890
Shall I prepare the 
horses for battle?

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.440
We will not be needing them.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.840
We are awaiting siege.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:44.250
Is that so?

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:50.040
Awaiting siege, huh? Boring.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.540
I had been hoping such a fool

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.690
would come up with something 
more interesting.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.880
So much

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:04.060
for our Nobunaga.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:16.230
<i>The Oda family is awaiting siege.</i>

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.720
<i>Move out with confidence.</i>

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.770
My lord?

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.080
You will catch cold, 
sleeping in a place like this.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:38.320
Return to your room, please!

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:52.350
Don't worry, you can 
go get some sleep.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:07:00.120
The maids were saying that we'd be sieged.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:03.720
Yet here you are, my lord,

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.140
seemingly waiting for something.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.240
Yeah, I am. I'm waiting.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:17.540
So you do have a plan!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:22.110
It seemed unlike you 
to simply hide in the castle.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:26.450
Well, we can't just wait in 
the castle, can we?

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:32.410
We have to win 
against Imagawa-san.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:38.310
My lord!

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:41.630
A mounted messenger has arrived.

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.620
The Marune and Washizu fortresses

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:45.320
have been surrounded 
by Imagawa forces.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:47.440
They are under attack.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.190
At the head of the Imagawa forces is the Mikawa army,

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:53.160
led by Motoyasu Matsudaira.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.500
Motoyasu Matsudaira?

00:07:56.550 --> 00:07:58.300
Isn't that...

00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.100
My lord!

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.040
A man named "Leader" is outside the gates,
 demanding to meet with you.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.260
Leader?!

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.460
We have no time for that.
 Turn him away.

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.940
It's about time!

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.660
My lord!

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:20.740
What is he thinking, 
at such a time?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:22.950
He intends to win.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:29.690
The lord intends to win against 
Imagawa's army of forty thousand.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:32.650
Tsune-chan!

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:35.850
What's keeping you? Hurry up!

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.030
We're moving out!

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:48.840
Oh, hey.

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:52.460
My lord, where are you going?

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:55.010
Are we not awaiting siege?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.690
I never said we'd be 
awaiting siege.

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:04.140
But—

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:13.910
Oh! Nobunaga-sama!

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.530
Hey, leader! Any news?

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:21.600
Sir, Yoshimoto Imagawa 
is at Kutsukake Castle.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.660
The men there say that they 
will move out at dawn.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.540
I suspect that if we leave now,

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:30.710
we will encounter them either 
at Dengakuhazama or Okehazama.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.250
Okehazama?

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:36.900
Wasn't there a 
"Battle of Okehazama"?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.460
Like, a famous one.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:40.350
I do not know.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:42.060
Whatever.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:42.970
Also,

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:46.440
Imagawa's men believe that the Oda 
family will be awaiting siege.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:49.710
Yeah? Good job finding that out.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.270
Thanks.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:53.360
We have our villagers 
in the Imagawa army.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.530
We will let you know as soon 
as we learn something new.

00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.360
You sure are dependable.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:09:59.480
Open the gate!

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:03.520
Oh, and, we knew 
it would be dark,

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.920
so the villagers 
prepared torches.

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.300
You're so thoughtful!

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.170
My lord!

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.420
Are we making a surprise attack?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.840
I knew you would not await siege.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:28.620
Everyone, forget that 
we're outnumbered!

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:32.560
If we take down their 
general, we win.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.320
Don't even look at the others.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.120
We're only after one man:

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.490
General

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:45.930
Yoshimoto Imagawa!

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:53.460
Impossible.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.630
Take down Yoshimoto?

00:10:56.290 --> 00:10:57.890
He could not.

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:01.690
There is no way 
Nobunaga could win!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:05.060
Nobunaga-sama!

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:06.930
Protect Owari!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:10.600
Shibata-sama, the lord 
has gone into battle.

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.020
What?

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:13.310
What did you say?

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:16.690
Sir, the lord has gone into battle.

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:18.890
Into battle?

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:20.740
It can't be...

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.400
We are going to the castle.

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:26.100
Sir!

00:11:27.070 --> 00:11:29.750
The lord has moved out. Hurry!

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:31.250
Prepare the horses.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:36.410
No... calm down.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:39.730
Surprise attacks don't 
succeed that easily.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.860
I doubt Imagawa 
would be taken down.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.350
Wait, my lord!

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.070
What?

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:58.940
There is no way we can go 
to war with just five men.

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.320
I beg you to wait for the others.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:02.900
Huh?

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:06.370
Oh, wow, there's actually 
only five of us.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.200
Why didn't they come along?

00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:15.380
Because you were so 
quick to move out.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.220
Whatever.

00:12:25.820 --> 00:12:29.220
I'll just take a nap 
while we wait.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.520
What is going on?

00:12:33.780 --> 00:12:36.130
Were we not awaiting siege?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.180
We could not possibly win 
in battle against Imagawa.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:40.600
Does the lord intend 
to end the Oda family?

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:44.860
We will accomplish nothing
 if we argue here.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.060
Shibata-dono.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:52.810
If our lord has moved out,
then we must follow him.

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:59.740
But we may die in vain, entering 
a battle we cannot win.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:04.170
The supreme commander 
of the Oda family is Nobunaga-sama!

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:11.460
If our lord chooses war,
then I will follow him.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:13.150
Excuse me.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.110
Tsune-chan...

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.030
Are you awake?

00:13:24.850 --> 00:13:29.540
You know, armor's not 
really good for sleeping in.

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:33.930
It's heavy, and stiff,
 and painful.

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:36.760
It was so uncomfortable.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.670
That would be obvious.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.380
Look at everyone who showed up 
while I was asleep!

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:50.050
All right, let's get going.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:53.770
Who's there?

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:56.690
I am not a threat.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.180
Hey, leader.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.110
Any news?

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:07.580
Imagawa's main army 
is preparing to rest.

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.820
Their general, Yoshimoto Imagawa,
 is there as well.

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:12.080
Where?

00:14:12.680 --> 00:14:14.120
Dengakuhazama.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.430
Got it.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.110
Thanks a lot.

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:21.060
You can go back to your village.

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:22.060
Right!

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.770
Well, then.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.390
Now that we know where we're 
headed, let's get going.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:36.880
Everyone, stay with me this time!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.660
Have we found the lord?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:00.750
No, not yet.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.530
Then find him!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.460
Shibata-sama.

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:09.970
Have we found the lord?

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.300
Yes, just now, 
at Dengakuhazama...

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.560
No... has he fallen?

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:23.740
He has defeated 
Yoshimoto Imagawa!

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.690
He defeated Imagawa.

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:34.910
Mouri-san!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:35.620
Sir!

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:42.050
To think that he defeated Imagawa.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:46.670
To think that there was such a meaning 
behind "eat well, sleep well."

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:51.700
Indeed, we should have known.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:56.610
There may have been spies 
among our men.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:04.400
The lord was so careful, 
he took that into consideration.

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:08.710
<i>Yoshimoto...</i>

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.900
<i>It was a mistake to think the 
Oda family would await siege.</i>

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:18.410
<i>Nobunaga would not 
consider such a thing.</i>

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:27.150
<i>It appears that 
I have underestimated him.</i>

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:32.310
Argh!

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:41.520
What is this?

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:51.230
Have you betrayed us?

00:16:53.350 --> 00:16:56.560
Yoshimoto had placed his trust in you.

00:16:57.020 --> 00:17:00.530
You said they would await siege,
 and he believed you.

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:03.470
What are you trying to say?

00:17:03.470 --> 00:17:06.470
You deliberately delivered 
false information

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:11.380
to put Yoshimoto off-guard
 and assist Nobunaga's attack.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.920
Is that not the most 
straightforward thinking?

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:25.600
Is it not, Tokichiro?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:31.320
Yeah. I suppose it is.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:33.440
Hey! Leader!

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:34.380
Hey!

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:37.110
Come on up.

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:46.080
It was thanks to their accurate information
that our surprise attack was successful.

00:17:46.640 --> 00:17:52.640
So I'm going to give the leader,
 Masa-kun, a reward.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:59.300
Masa-kun's a farmer, so he doesn't 
have an official last name.

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:01.860
So the two of us thought it over,
 and decided for you.

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:02.960
Here it is!

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.190
My name is Masatsuna Yanada.

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.510
Pretty cool, right?

00:18:12.510 --> 00:18:16.800
Oh, and I'm giving you land, 
so split it among yourselves.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.200
I understand that his 
information was useful,

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:24.450
but he's giving the most glory to a farmer
who was not even in the battle...

00:18:25.340 --> 00:18:34.550
He may be even more brilliant 
than we had imagined.

00:18:31.120 --> 00:18:32.190
Good job!

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.550
Goood jooob!

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:41.140
Ugh...

00:18:43.170 --> 00:18:45.660
That hurts.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:49.080
But this is convenient.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:54.590
Now there is no one on Imagawa's 
side that knows my face.

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:02.210
So I will establish myself 
on the Oda side.

00:19:03.090 --> 00:19:05.080
Nobunaga...

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:09.880
Someday, I will avenge myself 
for this humiliation.

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:13.960
I will obliterate the Oda family!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:25.770
And then, when I was surrounded 
by the Imagawa soldiers,

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:29.470
I ignored them and charged on.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:43.810
Do you really want 
to be here now?

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.500
Huh? Yeah.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.830
I told them I was tired, 
so I'm going to bed.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:52.940
Oh, hey, I knew it was here. 
Battle of Okehazama.

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:55.820
I thought it sounded familiar.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:20:03.340
"1560: Nobunaga Oda defeats 
Yoshimoto Imagawa at Okehazama."

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:05.950
Huh?

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.780
Oh, it talks about 
Imagawa-san here.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:11.030
Oh!

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:15.230
Was today's battle the 
Battle of Okehazama?

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:20.230
I just made history.

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:21.820
Wow...

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:22.960
My lord?

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:23.830
Huh?

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:28.650
But it was at Dengakuhazama, 
not Okehazama.

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.790
Ah, who cares about the details.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.290
I'm done studying.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:37.810
I'm tired. I'm going to sleep.

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.270
Good night.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:44.410
Good night.

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:49.010
He is already asleep.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.780
I am glad you are safe.
